    "q-143289": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143289",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{25}∼N(9,{15}^{2})$ is a random sample of size $25$ from a normal population, calculate $P(\\overset{―}{X}<9.08).$\n\n*Hint: A value table of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5040\\,$ | $\\,0.5080\\,$ | $\\,0.5120\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5438\\,$ | $\\,0.5478\\,$ | $\\,0.5517\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ | $\\,0.5910\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(9,\\frac{{15}^{2}}{25}) \\\\  & ∼N(9,9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're required to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}<9.08).$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}<9.08) & =P(Z<\\frac{9.08-9}{\\sqrt{9}}) \\\\  & =P(Z<0.03) \\\\  & =Φ(0.03)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.03)=0.5120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}<9.08) & =Φ(0.03) \\\\  & =0.5120.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
