    "q-143454": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143454",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The scores in a standardized math test used for university admissions in a certain country are normally distributed with a mean of $57$ and a standard deviation of $16.$ Suppose $50$ test results are selected at random. What is the probability that the mean score for this sample will be less than $55?$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1469\\,$ | $\\,0.1446\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.1379\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1711\\,$ | $\\,0.1685\\,$ | $\\,0.1660\\,$ | $\\,0.1635\\,$ | $\\,0.1611\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.1977\\,$ | $\\,0.1949\\,$ | $\\,0.1922\\,$ | $\\,0.1894\\,$ | $\\,0.1867\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\n then the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nWe're told that the population mean $\\mu =57$ the population standard deviation $\\sigma =16,$ and that the sample size $n=50.$ Therefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(57,\\frac{{16}^{2}}{50}) \\\\  & ∼N(57,5.12).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're required to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}<55).$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}<55) & =P(Z<\\frac{55-57}{\\sqrt{5.12}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z<-0.88) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.88)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.88)=0.1894.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}<55) & ≈Φ(-0.88) \\\\  & =0.1894.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
